{"format":"shim/composition-1","name":"Crate","manifest":{"format":"composition/1","name":"Crate","entry":"index.html","hosts":[{"host":"soundeo.com","endpoints":[{"method":"POST","path":"/tracks/favor/{id}"}]},{"host":"geo-samples.beatport.com"},{"host":"covers.sndstatic.com"},{"host":"preview.sndstatic.com"},{"host":"soundcloud.com"},{"host":"a-v2.sndcdn.com"},{"host":"api-v2.soundcloud.com"},{"host":"i1.sndcdn.com"},{"host":"wave.sndcdn.com"},{"host":"playback.media-streaming.soundcloud.cloud"},{"host":"api.beatport.com","mint":{"url":"https://www.beatport.com/api/auth/session","tokenPath":"token.accessToken","header":"Authorization","scheme":"Bearer","expiresPath":"token.accessTokenExpires"}},{"host":"geo-media.beatport.com"},{"host":"www.youtube.com"},{"host":"i.ytimg.com"},{"host":"www.1001tracklists.com","endpoints":[{"method":"POST","path":"/search/result.php"}]}],"connections":[{"name":"shared","engine":"supabase","storage":{"tables":[{"name":"playlists","columns":[{"name":"id","type":"text"},{"name":"kind","type":"text"},{"name":"name","type":"text"},{"name":"owner","type":"text"},{"name":"forked_from","type":"text"},{"name":"created_at","type":"text"},{"name":"updated_at","type":"text"},{"name":"updated_by","type":"text"},{"name":"deleted_at","type":"text"}]},{"name":"playlist_tracks","columns":[{"name":"playlist_id","type":"text"},{"name":"track_key","type":"text"},{"name":"track","type":"text"},{"name":"position","type":"real"},{"name":"added_by","type":"text"},{"name":"added_at","type":"text"},{"name":"moved_by","type":"text"},{"name":"color","type":"integer"},{"name":"color_by","type":"text"},{"name":"energy","type":"real"},{"name":"energy_by","type":"text"},{"name":"note","type":"text"},{"name":"note_by","type":"text"},{"name":"removed_at","type":"text"},{"name":"removed_by","type":"text"},{"name":"updated_at","type":"text"}]},{"name":"comments","columns":[{"name":"id","type":"text"},{"name":"playlist_id","type":"text"},{"name":"track_key","type":"text"},{"name":"author","type":"text"},{"name":"body","type":"text"},{"name":"created_at","type":"text"}]},{"name":"activity","columns":[{"name":"id","type":"integer"},{"name":"at","type":"text"},{"name":"actor","type":"text"},{"name":"verb","type":"text"},{"name":"playlist_id","type":"text"},{"name":"track_key","type":"text"},{"name":"detail","type":"text"}]},{"name":"track_links","columns":[{"name":"a","type":"text"},{"name":"b","type":"text"},{"name":"kind","type":"text"},{"name":"made_by","type":"text"},{"name":"detail","type":"text"},{"name":"updated_at","type":"text"}]},{"name":"track_notes","columns":[{"name":"track_ref","type":"text"},{"name":"author_id","type":"text"},{"name":"author","type":"text"},{"name":"title","type":"text"},{"name":"body","type":"text"},{"name":"tags","type":"text"},{"name":"created_at","type":"text"},{"name":"updated_at","type":"text"}]}]}}]},"files":[{"path":"actions.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"app.css","contentType":"text/css","contentBase64":""},{"path":"app.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"beatport.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"bpm.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"collections.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"columns.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"components.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"index.html","contentType":"text/html","contentBase64":""},{"path":"links.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"overlays.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"player.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"playerbar.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"safe.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"shared.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"soundcloud.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"soundeo.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"state.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"store.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"theme.css","contentType":"text/css","contentBase64":""},{"path":"tracklists.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"util.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"views.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""},{"path":"youtube.js","contentType":"text/javascript","contentBase64":""}],"authoringHistory":[{"role":"user","content":"Build Crate: one search across your music sources (Soundeo first), merged into one row per track, with a persistent player (waveform, seek, media keys), private notes, tags, playlists and sets."},{"role":"assistant","content":"First cut of Crate: the app shell from the design handoff (top bar, sidebar, player bar, keyboard overlay) and Soundeo search, preview playback with a page-built waveform, Media Session, private notes and tags, and local playlists and sets with colour, energy and Camelot hints. A checkpoint before testing search and playback end to end."},{"role":"user","content":"Build Crate: one search across your music sources (Soundeo first), merged into one row per track, with a persistent player (waveform, seek, media keys), private notes, tags, playlists and sets."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Crate phase 1 working against live Soundeo: search merges 100 hits into one row per track; BPM and Camelot key fill in for on-screen rows (paced, cached); ⏎ plays the 2:00 preview through the media route with a waveform you can click to seek; add-to palette creates playlists; playlist view, fork to set, and the set builder with key/BPM compatibility and transition notes all verified in the preview. Layout now fits windows down to ~1000px."},{"role":"user","content":"Add your Soundeo favorites to Crate as a source list you can browse, play, tag and add to playlists, the first of the per-source collections (SoundCloud likes and Beatport playlists later)."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Added Soundeo favorites: a \"From your sources\" section in the sidebar opens your Soundeo favorites (56 tracks, read live from soundeo.com/account/favorites, following pagination if it grows) as a read-only list you can play, tag, sort and add to your own playlists and sets, with Refresh (R) and Open on Soundeo. Search results now mark tracks that are in your favorites with a ♥. BPM/key lookups now fill rows top-down."},{"role":"user","content":"Fix Soundeo favorites that fail to play (\"no supported source\"): find which preview hosts those tracks use and make them playable."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed Soundeo favorites that wouldn't play: 46 of 56 use Soundeo's own preview host (preview.sndstatic.com, now declared and allowed), not Beatport's. Those links are signed and expire after about 3 days, so the player now fetches a fresh link from the track's Soundeo page when a link is stale or fails to load, and saves it back into your playlists; waveforms are cached by the unsigned path so a refreshed link reuses them. Verified a sndstatic favorite plays with its waveform; the expired-link refresh path wasn't exercised, since no link has expired yet."},{"role":"user","content":"Show each track's genre as a column in search, favorites and playlists."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Added a GENRE column (from Soundeo's listing and track details) to search, Soundeo favorites and playlists, with the full name on hover when it's cut off. Verified on your 56 favorites."},{"role":"user","content":"Add the shared space: playlists, sets, comments and an activity feed in the group's Supabase project, with polling for friends' changes."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Added the shared space (not yet connected): a \"shared\" Supabase connection for the group's project, with playlists, sets, per-playlist colour/energy/transition notes, comments and an activity log living there once it's configured. Crate polls the activity log (5s on screen, 30s hidden), highlights friends' edits as they arrive without moving your focus, adds an Activity tab with unread counts, comments in the details panel (C), and a Settings button to copy local playlists up. Without the connection everything stays local, as before."},{"role":"user","content":"Add the shared space: playlists, sets, comments and an activity feed in the group's Supabase project, with polling for friends' changes."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Shared space connected and reading: Crate finds the group's Supabase project, shows \"Shared · synced\", prompts for a display name, and offers to copy local playlists up. Settings buttons keep their natural width. Writes still to be exercised once the session ends."},{"role":"user","content":"Fix the list scroll jumping back to the top while you scroll (re-renders reset it)."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed lists jumping back to the top while you scroll: re-renders (BPM/key filling in, polls, saves) no longer scroll the focused row into view, a rebuild of the same screen keeps its scroll position, and shared-space updates only rebuild the screens that show shared data. Verified in favorites: scroll position and focus held through row updates and a full rebuild."},{"role":"user","content":"Make colour, energy and comments usable with the mouse (clickable stars, swatch, comment column, panel controls) and explain them in search and favorites."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Colour, energy and comments now work with the mouse: click a playlist row's stars to set energy (half steps; click the same value to clear), its swatch for a colour picker, and its CMT cell to open comments. The details panel shows the track's colour and energy in the open playlist with clickable swatches and stars. In search and favorites, the colour/energy/comment keys explain that these live inside a playlist instead of doing nothing. Verified the clicks reach the shared database (refused only while held by this session)."},{"role":"user","content":"Add SoundCloud to Crate: search merged into the same rows, full-length playback where allowed, its waveforms, and your SoundCloud likes as a source list."},{"role":"assistant","content":"An external session ended — its uncommitted changes were discarded."},{"role":"user","content":"Test whether SoundCloud's HLS streams can play in Crate (playlist rewritten in the page, chunks through the media route) before changing Shim."},{"role":"assistant","content":"An external session ended — its uncommitted changes were discarded."},{"role":"user","content":"Check SoundCloud HLS plays straight through Shim's media route (PR #733), then add SoundCloud search, playback and waveforms to Crate."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Added SoundCloud: search fans out to Soundeo and SoundCloud at once and merges into the same rows (SoundCloud rows show — for BPM/key, or a BPM read from the title as 128?); SoundCloud tracks play as full streams straight through the media route's HLS support (needs Shim with PR #733), with waveforms from SoundCloud's own data; a Soundeo preview is used only when SoundCloud has just a snippet. Sidebar and Settings show both sources' status, errors show per source, and SoundCloud Likes appear under From your sources once your profile name is set in Settings. Saved tracks keep a SoundCloud placeholder rather than a signed link that expires. Verified: merged search (150 hits → 113 rows) and a 72-minute SoundCloud stream playing with its waveform."},{"role":"user","content":"Add Beatport to Crate: merged search with BPM/key/ISRC, preview playback, and your Beatport playlists in the sidebar."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Added Beatport as a third source. Search now fans out to Soundeo, Beatport and SoundCloud together and merges the same track into one row (by ISRC, then the shared geo-samples preview file, then artist/title/mix), with Beatport supplying BPM and Camelot key. Your Beatport playlists appear under \"From your sources\" with track counts, open as read-only lists, and play Beatport previews with a waveform. Copy that said Soundeo-only is now source-neutral. Uses the token Beatport's own site mints from your signed-in session; the page never sees it."},{"role":"user","content":"Add a ♥ toggle in Crate that favorites/unfavorites a track on Soundeo, so Favorites can be curated from Crate."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Added a Soundeo ♥ toggle. Press L on any track row, click the ♥ next to a title, or use the ♡/♥ button in the details panel. It calls POST /tracks/favor/:id exactly like soundeo.com's own button (empty body, a toggle whose answer gives the new state). Crate trusts that answer, never sends two at once for a track, updates every copy of the track on screen, and re-reads Favorites the next time it's opened. Clear toasts for being refused, not signed in, or Soundeo saying no. Long titles now shrink so the ♥ and tags stay visible. Note: until Shim matches templated write paths (PR in progress), the call is refused as write-not-granted."},{"role":"user","content":"Friend onboarding for Crate: a setup checklist, a required display name before any shared write, and invite steps in Settings."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Friend onboarding. A \"Getting set up\" checklist (display name, shared space, Soundeo, Beatport, SoundCloud) shows each item's real state and the exact fix. It sits on the Dig home screen until a name and the shared space are set (it can be hidden), and always at the top of Settings. Nothing is written to the shared space under the placeholder name \"Me\" any more: an unnamed shared write (create, rename, add, move, colour, energy, note, comment, copy to shared) opens the name prompt with a toast and sends nothing. Settings → Share Crate now lists the steps to bring a friend in. Also fixed a crash when a shared playlist create is refused."},{"role":"user","content":"Fix the energy stars in the playlist table showing ~3.5 when the rating is 3 (the star widget stretched to the column width)."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Fixed the energy stars in the playlist table: the star widget stretched to the Energy column's width, so its percentage fill showed ~3.5 stars for a rating of 3 and skewed half-star clicks. It now shrink-wraps its five stars (width: max-content), matching the side panel."},{"role":"user","content":"Add match fixes: split a wrongly joined source off a row, join rows that are the same track (M), shared with the group through a new track_links table."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Match fixes. Each source in the track panel shows why it joined the row (ISRC match, same preview, name match, joined by hand) and has a ✂ button that splits it off into its own row. In search, the panel suggests likely matches (same title, from another source) with Join, and M joins selected rows. Fixes are stored per source track pair in the shared space's new track_links table (on this machine when it's off), so later searches and friends get them. Each fix can be undone from the panel, and fixes appear in Activity under \"Match fixes\". The source chips also open the panel by mouse now."},{"role":"user","content":"Add Find versions: from any track, search every source for its remixes, edits, bootlegs and VIPs, grouped by kind."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Find versions: a panel button and the V key search every source for a track's lead artist and title, and show only rows with that title, grouped as Original & cuts, Remixes, Edits, bootlegs & VIPs, and Same title, other artists, with the original row focused and an All results button. Also collapses a source's duplicate listings of one recording (re-releases, compilations) back into one row, which v44 had started showing separately, unless a fix split them."},{"role":"user","content":"Shared track notes: move private notes into the shared space (track_notes table, one note per person per source track), show other people's notes in the track panel, add a stable author id."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Track notes move to the shared space: one note per person per source track in the new track_notes table, with a Keep private switch per note. The track panel shows the group's notes, rows with a note get a pencil, and Settings shows the id your notes are filed under."},{"role":"user","content":"Show notes inline in the track tables as a Notes column, and add a Columns picker to choose which columns each table shows."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Notes show inline: a Notes column in the search, source and playlist tables (your note, or the group's when you have none; click it to write). A Columns button on each table picks which columns show."},{"role":"user","content":"Let table columns be reordered by dragging their headings and resized by dragging a heading's right edge."},{"role":"assistant","content":"Table columns can be reordered (drag a heading) and resized (drag a heading's right edge; double-click it to reset). The Columns picker lists them in your order and can reset order and widths."},{"role":"user","content":"Add YouTube as a search source: results from youtube.com merge into the table, with a link that opens the video in a tab (no playback in Crate)."},{"role":"assistant","content":"YouTube is a source now: every search also reads youtube.com's results (videos only) and merges them into the table with a YT chip. YouTube doesn't play in Crate; the panel's Open link opens the video in a tab and shows the channel, views and age."},{"role":"user","content":"Add DJ play counts and a freshness label from 1001tracklists, a Remixes on SoundCloud button, and BPM-matched suggestions for a playlist"},{"role":"assistant","content":"DJ plays and a freshness label from 1001tracklists (columns, sort, panel), Remixes on SoundCloud (⇧V), tempo- and genre-matched suggestions for a playlist (U); dragged column widths give way before Artist and Title"},{"role":"user","content":"Measure a track's BPM from its audio when no source lists one"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Measure a track’s BPM from its audio when no source lists one (shown as 87?): during a preview’s waveform pass, or a short silent pass on a SoundCloud stream when it plays or its details open"},{"role":"user","content":"Read-only: look up the tracks of a rekordbox playlist on Soundeo, Beatport and SoundCloud (nothing will be committed)"},{"role":"assistant","content":"An external session ended — its uncommitted changes were discarded."},{"role":"user","content":"Make the display-name placeholder neutral before Crate is published"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Neutral placeholder in the display-name prompt"},{"role":"user","content":"Check every link on a saved track before Crate follows it (tracks from the shared space are other people's data)"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Check every link on a saved track before following it: tracks from the shared space keep only links that point where their source can (safe.js)"},{"role":"user","content":"Tighten the saved-track link check: refuse media paths the browser would tidy into a different host"},{"role":"assistant","content":"Refuse saved media paths the browser would tidy into a different host (dot segments, encoded dots, backslashes)"}]}